From: Backported from bash 5.2
Subject: Fix get_arg parameter order in mkbuiltins.c

The get_arg function signature had parameters in wrong order relative
to how all callers used it. This was caught by GCC 14+ which treats
incompatible pointer types as errors.

Fixed in bash 5.2 by swapping parameters 2 and 3 to match callers.

--- a/builtins/mkbuiltins.c
+++ b/builtins/mkbuiltins.c
@@ -744,8 +744,8 @@ strip_whitespace (string)
 char *
 get_arg (
      char *for_whom,
-     char *string,
-     DEF_FILE *defs
+     DEF_FILE *defs,
+     char *string
 )
 {
